  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material implying a deceptive business venture",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'only sells shakes' as the target of the meme's ironic commentary. The user imagines themselves as the consumer or observer who is deceived by the business's misleading name ('ice cream shop') and disappointing product offering ('only sells shakes'). This projection is implicit, as the meme does not use explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the humor and critique are directed at the user's perception of the business's dishonesty or subpar quality. The user is thus projected onto the textual punchline, which represents the core of the meme's ironic message.",
